  "quote_of_the_week": {
    "type": "Quote of the Week",
    "quote": "If you don't lose, you can't enjoy victories. You have to accept both things.",
    "author": "Rafael Nadal (born 03 June 1986) - Spanish former professional tennis player, winner of 22 Grand Slams."
  },
  "market_commentary": {
    "overview": "",
    "bulkers": "Two Greek-controlled capesize units have changed hands this week; EPIC (182k dwt built \n2010 at Odense/Denmark) sold for approximately $32.2-$32.8 million to clients of Mercuria while \nCAPE BRAZIL (178k dwt built at SWS/China) was acquired from Far Eastern buyers for $31.5 \nmillion. In the active Ultramax arena, Turkish buyers purchased the eco unit BERGE TATEYAMA \n(63.5k dwt built 2020 at Shin Kasado/Japan) for $34.25 million. Singaporean owners of ONLY YOU \n(60.5k dwt built 2017 at Sanoyas/Japan) made a significant profit, selling her for $28.3 million after \nbuying her seven months ago for just $23.2 million. The one-year older sister vessel NORD \nCHESAPEAKE (60.5k dwt built at Sanoyas/Japan) commanded the price of $25.5 million, while \nEXPLORER AMERICA (61.7k built 2011 at Ohima/Japan) was purchased by Chinese interests for \n$18.2 million, both with surveys pending. TESS 58 FORTUNE TIGER (built 2013 at \nCebu/Philippines) sold for $19 million and same age Crown 58 HAI JIN (built 2013 at Dayang/China) \nfor just under $16 million. The box-shaped supramax SSI ERDOGAN BEY (51k dwt built 2010 \nOshima/Japan) achieved $15 million with surveys recently passed. Chinese buyers paid $9 million for \nDiamond 53 Supramax SPAR LIBRA (53k dwt built 2006 at Chengxi/China), same level as her sister \nSPAR CANIS was sold end of last month. Chinese-controlled OASIS CHAMPION (50k dwt built \n2002 at Mitsui/Japan) found buyers that spent $7.5 million, aligned with the recent sale of MARIA F \n(52k dwt built 2002 at Sanoyas/Japan) for $7.8 mill after surveys. Following last week's reported sale \nof POWAN, clients of Swire have also agreed to sell her sister vessel HUNAN (B-Delta design 39k \ndwt built 2016 at Chengxi/China, box, tier-2) for a similar price of $19 million to undisclosed buyers. \nAnother B-Delta sister-ship SIDER ATHENA (39k dwt built 2013 at Chengxi/China, box, Tier-2) was \nsold for $16 million. Meanwhile RADIANT WEB (38k dwt built 2012 at Shimanami/Japan, open \nhatch) found Greek buyers that paid $15.3 million following recently passed dry-docking surveys. The \nvintage logger LIBERATOR (28k dwt built 2006 at Shimanami/Japan) achieved $6.7 million with \nsurveys due, outperforming the December deal of similar vessel CSE PROSPERITY EXPRESS (28k \ndwt built 2006 at Imabari/Japan), which was sold for $5.5 mill, with surveys also pending.",
    "tankers": "Greek Owners have been active this week in both buying and selling: Clients of Thenamaris \nacquired the scrubber-fitted Suezmax sister vessels EMERALDWAY & SUNRISEWAY (158k dwt \nbuilt 2022 at SWS/China) for $177 million en bloc. Meanwhile the older unit FAIRWAY (160k dwt \nbuilt 2013 at HHIC/Philippines) was sold for $56.5 million to clients of Metrostar. Clients of \nPerformance committed their aframax vessel P. SOPHIA (105k dwt built 2009 at Hyundai/South \nKorea) for $36.5 million basis forward delivery mid-May - mid June to undisclosed interests. Greek \nbuyers also purchased two panamax vessels, AGILE (74k dwt built 2007 at New Times/China) & \nPGC ALEXANDRIA (75k dwt built 2006 at Onomichi/Japan) for $13.5 million & $15.75 million, \nrespectively.",
    "demolition": "Subcontinent rates remain stable with a positive sentiment due to high tonnage demand \nbut low supply. For an overview of demolition market rates, please check our comprehensive \ndemometer below:"
  },
